-- title:
--   Is Proj Kronecker
-- statement:
--   **Kronecker products preserve projectivity.** Let `A` and `B` be projectors on two finite Hilbert spaces. Their Kronecker product is again a self-adjoint idempotent operator:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{IsProj}(A)\land\operatorname{IsProj}(B)
--   \Longrightarrow
--   \operatorname{IsProj}(A\otimes B),
--   \qquad (A\otimes B)^2=A\otimes B.
--   $$
--
--   The statement supplies the basic tensor-product closure used when building enlarged measurements and auxiliary projectors from local projective effects.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.isProj_kronecker`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective/NaimarkCore.lean#L62-L80

